I pulled the remote changes into `main`. The branches had diverged, so I merged them instead of rebasing, and the merge completed with no conflicts. I haven't run the tests or the app after the merge.

The remote brought in 70 files (about 10.9k lines added), including:
- a new `pm_copilot/` backend package (the decision API, agents, evidence and store modules);
- a new plain JS/CSS frontend (`frontend/app.js`, `workspace.js`, `styles.css`);
- updates to the React components;
- new tests for the decision modules;
- docs and PRDs, plus `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and the `.claude/` and `.codex/` settings.

`main` is now two commits ahead of `origin/main`: your local commit and the merge commit. I haven't pushed.
